# One free name read by one path, two candidates of different layouts at two calls: rd reads a3\x, a3 declared after
# it; the root hands its a3 (Model, x at 0), go its own (Wide, x at 1).  The coordinate space is the first declaration
# that reaches the input; each candidate is admitted to it where its call forms the input, so neither the first
# candidate nor its record decides the slot of another.  Exit 7; 81-83 if a call read the wrong field.
Model:
    int: x 1
end: Model
Wide:
    int: pad 9
    int: x 2
end: Wide
fn: rd () int
    return: a3\x
end: rd
fn: go () int
    a3: merge: Wide
    return: rd()
end: go
a3: merge: Model
int: g1 rd()
int: g2 go()
int: g3 rd()
int: ok 7
if: g1 != 1
    ok: 81
if: g2 != 2
    ok: 82
if: g3 != 1
    ok: 83
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
